  "script": "Five ChatGPT features you're probably not using. Over one hundred fifty million people talk to ChatGPT out loud every week.\n\nIf that's not you, stick around. The other four live in Settings too. Voice got rebuilt this July into full duplex: listening and talking at once.\n\nTasks are hands-off too: run one-time or recurring, up to three active on free accounts. Paid plans get hourly scheduling and can watch things like Gmail for you.\n\nMemory doesn't wait to be asked. It remembers you across every chat, and this June OpenAI opened it to free accounts as well.\n\nData analysis works automatically: drop in a spreadsheet, get code, a chart, and answers. Free gets three uploads a day.\n\nAnd Projects pulls it together, chats, files, and instructions in one space, so ChatGPT stops starting from zero. Free gets five files, Plus twenty-five.\n\nSave this, then open Settings, and let them run without you.",
